# Accepted image findings, read by the Security scan workflow.
#
# Every entry needs a reason, an owner and an expiry date (`exp:YYYY-MM-DD`);
# Trivy ignores the entry again after that date, so an exception cannot rot
# silently. Keep this file short: the default is to fix, not to ignore.
#
# CVE-2026-47884 - spring-webmvc (transitive via spring-boot-starter-web).
#   Fixed only in Spring Framework 7.0.9, i.e. the Spring Boot 4 line. The
#   services run Boot 3.5 (Framework 6.2), where no patched release exists.
#   Mitigation: the services do not use Spring MVC template rendering or
#   view resolution over untrusted input; the impacted path is a remote
#   handling flaw in annotated controllers with data binding. Tracked as the
#   first item of the Boot 4 upgrade, which is required before production.
#   owner: @An619
CVE-2026-47884 exp:2026-12-31
#
# CVE-2026-65182 - tomcat-embed-core. The advisory names 10.1.58 as the fix but
#   that patch release is not published in Maven Central yet (10.1.55 is the
#   newest available). Tomcat is embedded and only serves the services' own
#   actuator/API endpoints behind the cluster network policy, so this is a
#   deferred patch, not a tolerated design flaw. Bump tomcat.version to 10.1.58
#   as soon as it resolves, and delete this line.
#   owner: @An619
CVE-2026-65182 exp:2026-12-15
